                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we use `networkctl {down,up} $IFACE` instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-anacapa/recipes-phosphor/network/phosphor-network/ncsi-bounce.sh",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "u8813345-amd",
                        "email": "colin.huang2@amd.com",
                        "username": "u8813345-amd"
                    },
                    "message": "1. `ip link set` control kernel netdev and `networkctl` will notify network manager to run dhcp etc.., This script is an oneshut service and run during bmc boot. The main task was to re-initialize the NCSI interface. If this is a time service, `networkctl` is better. \n2. `ip link set` this solution is verified by our FWV team.\n\nSo, I will keep to use 'ip link set'"
                },
